# [DD-13b.W23.1] `version` IS RESERVED, AND THE REFUSAL MUST SAY SO.
#
# A keyword with NO schema row refuses as an unknown token in its scope,
# which is the truth about a WITHDRAWN production and a LIE about a
# reserved one: `version` is a word the format owns and no build parses.
# So it has a row whose `wave` is the reserved sentinel, the same
# derivation that produces the "not in this build" list produces this
# too, and the refusal names the word rather than sending a reader
# hunting a typo in it (K14's shape).
#
# The reservation is one line of insurance against the day a change to
# this format is not additive. Nothing today is, which is why the keyword
# has a row and no production.
version 2
pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
